      {
        "id": "u2",
        "kind": "CONCEPT",
        "label": "Definition of the Mole and Avogadro's Number",
        "attributes": {
          "depth": "statement"
        },
        "subtopic_ids": [
          "s2"
        ],
        "rationale": "States the formal definition of the mole as representing 6.022 x 10^23 particles and introduces Avogadro's number.",
        "review_flags": [],
        "contextualization": {
          "value": "everyday",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "passage_id": "p14",
              "quote": "So, just like \"1 dozen\" always means 12 items (whether it's 12 eggs or 12 pencils):"
            }
          ]
        },
        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "p10",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "heading"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "## What is a Mole?",
            "start": 533,
            "end": 551
          },
          {
            "id": "p11",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "**A mole is simply a number** — a very large number that represents a fixed quantity of particles.",
            "start": 553,
            "end": 651
          },
          {
            "id": "p12",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "equation"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "$$\\boxed{1 \\text{ mole} = 6.022 \\times 10^{23} \\text{ particles}}$$",
            "start": 653,
            "end": 720
          },
          {
            "id": "p13",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "This number is called **Avogadro's Number** (or Avogadro's Constant), named after the Italian scientist Amedeo Avogadro.",
            "start": 722,
            "end": 842
          },
          {
            "id": "p14",
            "category": "ANALOGY",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "So, just like \"1 dozen\" always means 12 items (whether it's 12 eggs or 12 pencils):",
            "start": 844,
            "end": 927
          },
          {
            "id": "p15",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "**1 mole always means 6.022 × 10²³ particles** (whether it's atoms, molecules, ions, or electrons)",
            "start": 929,
            "end": 1027
          },
          {
            "id": "p16",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "separator"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "---",
            "start": 1029,
            "end": 1032
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "Accurately defines the mole as 6.022 x 10^23 entities (Avogadro's number) regardless of particle type.",
          "errors": []
        }
      },
      {
